					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ethanhanson" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4465845); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4465845&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605924404" alt="EthanHanson" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4465845)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ethanhanson" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4465845); return false;" >EthanHanson</a></span> <span class="odate time_1605919282 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">21 Nov 2020 00:41</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4824104">
									

<p>I was summoned by IRC Chat. Let's crit this.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Right of the bat, why don't you have the Seeking greenlight, Page Type, Genre, and Page Layout sections? Those don't add up to the word limit, and you should add them so reviewers know if you want greenlights, what type of page you want, what genre you're aiming for, etc.</p>
<p>Now, let's do the actual crit:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This humanoid makes any person they encounter a narcoleptic</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Please specify if the humanoid chooses a person or it just affects <em>anyone</em> they encounter. I think it would be difficult for it to affect <em>everyone</em>. And if they chooses a person, does the person need to have any characteristics or it's just random?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>they are lured into a sense of security before being murdered and/or eaten alive</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why? As I'm aware, the Ole Lukøje only punishes bad children. Why does this entity attacks people? Is it for food, fun, punishment&#8230;?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Central Narrative:</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So my concern with your narrative is that it seems to have an escessive amount of references to the original story of the Ole Lukøje. While you can write something based off a fairy tale, you need to put some kind of twist to it, otherwise it would be just the same thing with the SCP logo slapped to it.</p>
<p>&quot;The Ole Lukøje but now it's evil&quot; isn't a good twist, at leat on my perspective. It seems cliché to just take a character and make it evil for no reason. Maybe you could write <em>why</em> did the Ole Lukøje become evil? Maybe an interview with the entity could clarify this? Maybe the researchers recognize him from old folktales and they are curious on why he is killing people now?</p>
<p>The other thing that concerns me is that all of your narrative is backstory. It's not wrong to focus on the backstory, but the only thing you're telling is how it came to Foundation custody. What happened after? I think an interview with the entity could improve your story.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Also, the “it killed me and it’ll kill you again&quot; has no relation to what the SCP does after you wake up they were just spouting nonsense due to their new psychotic nature.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think MTF members would be a lot more calm when waking up of a dream like this. Sure, they're afraid to die, but they're trained to face things like this. Maybe they would be worried and nervous, but they wouldn't be screaming like that.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I like stories based off pieces of literature, but I think this needs some kind of in-deep twist to differentiate it from the original story.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look.</p>

							</div>

								
					
